{:org/id :org-global-football-supporters-branches
 :org/name "Official football supporters' club branches (penyes, Fanclubs, 後援会, peñas)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-fan-club
 :org/category :cat-sports
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-europe
 :org/countries ["ES" "DE" "GB" "IT" "JP" "AR" "BR" "MX" "US" "ID"]
 :org/founding-date 1920
 :org/instance-count-estimate 4753
 :org/member-count 339245
 :org/member-count-basis "source-pinned for two clubs: Bayern Munich recognises 4,753 fan clubs with 339,245 fan club members, of which 572 clubs in 108 countries are international with about 46,880 members; FC Barcelona's official penya census stood at 1,264 recognised supporters' clubs (2023). These are BRANCH counts recognised by the club, not the club's own membership — Bayern separately has 400,000+ club members, which is a different thing again."
 :org/proxy-metric "club-recognised branch registers"
 :org/proxy-bias "Counts only branches the club has formally recognised. Unrecognised supporter groups, ultras groups (recorded separately in this corpus) and the far larger population of unaffiliated fans are excluded by construction, so this undercounts organised support and says nothing about total fandom."
 :org/legal-registration :mixed
 :org/registration-note "Branches are typically registered associations in their own right (a German Fanclub is usually an e.V.) while being recognised by, not owned by, the club."
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "Local branches that organise travel to matches, run their own bar or clubhouse, hold an AGM and elect officers — a franchise of belonging, where a club's identity is reproduced by thousands of small associations it does not control."
 :org/related-org "org-esp-socios-clubs"
 :org/source-name "FC Bayern München fan club pages / FC Barcelona penyes census"
 :org/source-url "https://fcbayern.com/en/fans/fan-clubs/fanclubs"
 :org/source-date "2025"
 :org/source-tier :primary
 :org/source-caveat "Two clubs pinned; there is no global count of supporters' branches across football."
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-26"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

{:org/id :org-jpn-artist-fan-clubs
 :org/name "Subscription artist fan clubs (ファンクラブ, official fandom memberships)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-fan-club
 :org/category :cat-hobby-interest
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-asia-east
 :org/countries ["JP" "KR" "CN" "TW" "US" "GB"]
 :org/founding-date 1960
 :org/member-count-basis "source-pinned as an INFERRED figure, with the inference stated: Japanese agencies generally do NOT publish fan club membership. Fans reconstruct it from the sequential membership number issued at signup, and community-maintained rankings put STARTO ENTERTAINMENT (the former Johnny's) fan clubs at 14,587,100 as of 2025-01-25 including the Junior joho-kyoku. That figure is CUMULATIVE — it counts numbers ever issued, not current paying members — so it overstates the live community, by an unknown margin. Arashi still ranks first despite having stopped activity in 2020, which shows the same thing from another angle; Snow Man passed one million in 2023."
 :org/proxy-metric "sequential membership numbers issued at signup"
 :org/proxy-bias "Cumulative and unreconciled: lapsed members are never subtracted, one person may hold memberships in several groups, and a disbanded act keeps its number. The artefact grows monotonically while the actual community can shrink — structurally the same failure as counting cumulative blockchain addresses."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/registration-note "The fan club is operated by the agency as a paid service; the community is the members, who have no governance rights over it at all — the corpus's clearest case of a community owned by a counterparty."
 :org/governance-model :hierarchical
 :org/mission-statement "Paid memberships that allocate concert ticket lotteries, exclusive media and fan events — where a subscription is the entry to a community whose ranking, etiquette and seniority (by membership number) are entirely member-generated."
 :org/related-org "org-global-fandoms"
 :org/source-name "Community-maintained STARTO/Johnny's fan club membership rankings (agency does not publish)"
 :org/source-url "https://kuracon.jp/johnnys-fc-ranking/"
 :org/source-date "2025-01-25"
 :org/source-tier :secondary
 :org/source-caveat "No primary source exists by design: the agency withholds the figure, so every published number is a fan reconstruction from issued membership numbers."
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-26"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

